    @tableofcontents

    @section ssh2v200 ssh2 Module Version 2.0.0
    Major feature release closing all client-side feature gaps in the libssh2 wrapper.

    <b>Build and test support:</b>
    - documentation includes DataProvider and ConnectionProvider cross-references and corrected parameter names
    - SSH/SFTP test suites accept a named \c --uri option for isolated qualification servers
    - \c QORE_SSH2_STRICT_DOCS makes documentation warnings fail the build

    <b>Authentication Enhancements:</b>
    - added SSH agent authentication support; tried automatically before other methods
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setUseAgent() "SSH2Base::setUseAgent()")
    - added public key authentication from memory without temp files
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setKeysFromData() "SSH2Base::setKeysFromData()")

    <b>Security - Known Hosts Verification:</b>
    - <b>host key verification is now enabled by default</b> (secure by default) using the
      @ref Qore::SSH2::Ssh2HostKeyPolicy::TrustOnFirstUse policy and the local user's <tt>~/.ssh/known_hosts</tt> file
      (resolved automatically when filesystem access is permitted); this closes a
      man-in-the-middle vulnerability where the previous default silently connected to any server
      and could disclose credentials to an attacker
    - added known hosts file support for host key verification
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setKnownHostsFile() "SSH2Base::setKnownHostsFile()",
      @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setVerifyHostKey() "SSH2Base::setVerifyHostKey()")
    - configurable host key policy:
      @ref Qore::SSH2::Ssh2HostKeyPolicy::TrustOnFirstUse "TrustOnFirstUse" (default, persistent
      TOFU), @ref Qore::SSH2::Ssh2HostKeyPolicy::Reject "Reject", or
      @ref Qore::SSH2::Ssh2HostKeyPolicy::TrustOnFirstUseSession "TrustOnFirstUseSession"
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setHostKeyPolicy() "SSH2Base::setHostKeyPolicy()")
    - a configured known_hosts file that exists but cannot be read or parsed now causes the
      connection to fail with \c SSH2-HOSTKEY-ERROR instead of silently connecting without
      verification (fail closed)
    - verification-enabled persistent TOFU connections with no configured known_hosts file fail
      closed with \c SSH2-HOSTKEY-ERROR; set
      @ref Qore::SSH2::Ssh2HostKeyPolicy::TrustOnFirstUseSession "TrustOnFirstUseSession"
      explicitly for legacy session-only trust
    - the plaintext authentication password is no longer written to debug output
    - added process-global default controls for embedding applications where the OS user differs
      from the logical user and the OS user's <tt>~/.ssh/known_hosts</tt> must not be used:
      @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setDefaultVerifyHostKey() "SSH2Base::setDefaultVerifyHostKey()",
      @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setDefaultHostKeyPolicy() "SSH2Base::setDefaultHostKeyPolicy()",
      @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setDefaultKnownHostsFile() "SSH2Base::setDefaultKnownHostsFile()"
      (and corresponding \c getDefault*() methods), plus the \c QORE_SSH2_DEFAULT_VERIFY_HOST_KEY,
      \c QORE_SSH2_DEFAULT_HOST_KEY_POLICY, and \c QORE_SSH2_DEFAULT_KNOWN_HOSTS environment
      variables; see @ref embedding_multitenant
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::getHostKey() "SSH2Base::getHostKey()" returning MD5/SHA1/SHA256 fingerprints
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::addKnownHost() "SSH2Base::addKnownHost()" for manual host key management
    - added the @ref Qore::SSH2::Ssh2HostKeyPolicy "Ssh2HostKeyPolicy" enum and legacy
      \c SSH2_HOSTKEY_REJECT, \c SSH2_HOSTKEY_TOFU, and \c SSH2_HOSTKEY_TOFU_SESSION constants

    <b>Non-Blocking I/O:</b>
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient::startPollGetFile() "SFTPClient::startPollGetFile()", which
      returns an @ref Qore::AbstractPollOperation "AbstractPollOperation" object
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SftpPollOperation "SftpPollOperation") that retrieves a remote file without
      blocking the calling thread; the TCP connection, the SSH handshake, host key verification,
      authentication, and the transfer itself are all driven by the caller's poll loop, so an
      \c "sftp://" location can be read by an event loop or an I/O controller managing many
      connections at once
    - authentication policy and ordering and host key verification are shared with the blocking
      connect path, so blocking and non-blocking connections make identical security decisions
    - @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base "SSH2Base" objects are now
      @ref Qore::AbstractPollableIoObject "AbstractPollableIoObject" objects; the descriptor of the
      underlying connection is available with
      @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::getPollableDescriptor() "SSH2Base::getPollableDescriptor()"
    - a client running a poll operation is reserved for that operation; other operations on the
      same object fail with an \c SSH2-POLL-IN-PROGRESS exception until it completes, is aborted,
      or is destroyed
    - a poll operation that adopts an already-established connection that the server has since
      closed reestablishes it once and starts over, matching the implicit reconnection behavior of
      the blocking methods

    <b>Session Configuration:</b>
    - added algorithm preference control
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setMethodPreference() "SSH2Base::setMethodPreference()")
    - added supported algorithm query
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::getSupportedAlgorithms() "SSH2Base::getSupportedAlgorithms()")
    - added SSH banner control
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setBanner() "SSH2Base::setBanner()",
      @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::getBanner() "SSH2Base::getBanner()")
    - added configurable keepalive interval
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setKeepalive() "SSH2Base::setKeepalive()")
    - added debug/trace support with \c SSH2_TRACE_* constants
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setTraceLevel() "SSH2Base::setTraceLevel()")

    <b>Channel Operations:</b>
    - added PTY window resize support
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Channel::requestPtySize() "SSH2Channel::requestPtySize()")
    - added exit signal retrieval
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Channel::getExitSignal() "SSH2Channel::getExitSignal()")
    - added signal sending to remote processes
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Channel::sendSignal() "SSH2Channel::sendSignal()")
    - added SSH agent forwarding on channels
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Channel::requestAuthAgent() "SSH2Channel::requestAuthAgent()")
    - added Unix domain socket forwarding
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Client::openDirectStreamLocalChannel() "SSH2Client::openDirectStreamLocalChannel()")

    <b>Reverse Port Forwarding:</b>
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Listener "SSH2Listener" class for reverse port forwarding
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Client::forwardListen() "SSH2Client::forwardListen()" to create remote listeners
    - equivalent to \c "ssh -R" reverse tunneling

    <b>SFTP Operations:</b>
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient::symlink() "SFTPClient::symlink()" - create symbolic links
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient::readlink() "SFTPClient::readlink()" - read symlink targets
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient::lstat() "SFTPClient::lstat()" - stat without following symlinks
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient::chown() "SFTPClient::chown()" - change file ownership
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient::statvfs() "SFTPClient::statvfs()" - filesystem statistics

    <b>SCP Improvements:</b>
    - updated to use \c libssh2_scp_recv2() and \c libssh2_scp_send64() for proper 64-bit file size support

    <b>Data Provider Updates:</b>
    - added symlink, readlink, chown, lstat, and statvfs data providers

    <b>Connection Module Updates:</b>
    - added typed client identity provider and host-key store APIs backed by the
      @c sshutil module
    - added \c known_hosts, \c host_key_policy, \c verify_host_key, \c use_agent, and
      \c keepalive_interval connection options
    - added matching host-key verification options to the SFTP client data provider constructor
    - the \c verify_host_key connection option now defaults to @ref Qore::True "True" (secure by
      default), consistent with the underlying client classes

    <b>Bug Fixes:</b>
    - worked around a libssh2 defect that made
      @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient::symlink() "SFTPClient::symlink()" report every successful call as
      an error: libssh2 commit \c 2dae302 (the fix for \c CVE-2025-15661) reads the status code of
      the \c SSH_FXP_SYMLINK response at the offset of the request id, so a status of \c SSH_FX_OK
      is reported as \c LIBSSH2_ERROR_SFTP_PROTOCOL with the request id as the SFTP status code;
      the real status is unavailable on such a build, so the link is now verified against the server
      when libssh2 reports an SFTP protocol error, and the exception is raised only if the link does
      not resolve to the requested target.  Upstream fixed the defect in commit \c 4ed26f5, which is
      in no libssh2 release yet, while distributions have backported the CVE fix alone into 1.11.1;
      patched and unpatched builds report the same \c LIBSSH2_VERSION_NUM, so an affected library
      cannot be recognized from its version
    - removed stale TODO in mkdir implementation
    - documented known memory leak in sftp_shutdown timeout (libssh2 limitation)
    - updated copyright years to 2026

    @section ssh2v150 ssh Module Version 1.5.0
    - added support for interruptible I/O for graceful termination of sandboxed programs; interrupt
      checks are performed before socket connect operations
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/5116">issue 5116</a>)
    - added the @ref sftpclientdataproviderintro "SftpClientDataProvider user module"
    - added application action support for SFTP polling and SFTP client actions

    @section ssh2v142 ssh Module Version 1.4.2
    - fixed a bug where the \c sftp connection scheme was unusable
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4755">issue 4755</a>)

    @section ssh2v141 ssh Module Version 1.4.1
    - fixed a bug where the sftp event type was registered twice
